{"seq":1,"slug":"anatomy-physiology","title":"第一章 动物解剖与生理基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/anatomy-physiology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"musculoskeletal-system","title":"大学兽医学 — 骨骼肌肉与体表方位","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/anatomy-physiology/musculoskeletal-system","wordCount":1709,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"digestive-system","title":"大学兽医学 — 消化系统与反刍生理","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/anatomy-physiology/digestive-system","wordCount":1774,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"circulatory-respiratory","title":"大学兽医学 — 循环与呼吸系统","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/agriculture/veterinary/anatomy-physiology/circulatory-respiratory","wordCount":1752,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"# 第一章 动物解剖与生理基础\n\n解剖学回答\"动物身体由什么构成、各部分长在哪里\"，生理学回答\"这些结构如何工作、如何维持生命\"。这两者是兽医的\"地图\"与\"说明书\"——不认识正常的样子，就无法识别异常。\n\n本章从骨骼肌肉与体表结构入手，建立空间方位感；再深入消化、呼吸、循环等核心器官系统的运作原理；最后比较不同物种（如单胃的犬猫与多胃的牛羊）在结构上的关键差异，为后续的病理与临床打下坚实基础。\n"}